       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it could seriously harm the patient.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3000 mg/day. Above that, there is a risk of hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n- **Patient factors:** Normal liver and kidney function and a weight of 70 kg don't justify this dose.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (2600 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale. I would still want to know whether your institution's policy allows an override before I enter it.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
